{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5da99agWCYCWEZKjhd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `sqlmigrate` now only wraps its output in BEGIN/COMMIT when the migration is atomic and the database can roll back DDL. That is the same rule the migration executor already uses.\n\nThe fix is one line in `django/core/management/commands/sqlmigrate.py:60`:\n\n```python\nself.output_transaction = migration.atomic and connection.features.can_rollback_ddl\n```\n\nI also updated the comment above it to match.\n\nAll 88 tests in `migrations.test_commands` pass. That run doesn't actually test the new behavior, though: none of those tests set `can_rollback_ddl` to False. I didn't add the test the ticket suggests (mocking `can_rollback_ddl` to False) because the rules say not to edit test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":19672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215},"output_tokens":251,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a855459d-e5b7-4ed9-a264-29305570ba65","uuid":"7261783a-e07c-4282-9069-59a1f24ee25a","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:35:48.427Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5da1DrDgy7ceBBFjZr"}
